{
    "background_story": "Harlee was a free-spirited artist who preferred the unconventional path. Growing up in a family of traditional musicians, she was expected to follow in their footsteps. However, Harlee's heart belonged to the world of visual arts. She preferred the feel of paint on her fingertips and the smell of canvas to the sound of strings and drums. Despite her family's initial disappointment, Harlee pursued her passion, attending art school and eventually opening her own studio. Her unique style, which blended street art with fine art, quickly gained recognition in the local art scene. Harlee's preference for the unorthodox led her to create stunning murals that told stories of social justice and environmental awareness. Her art became a reflection of her values, inspiring others to think outside the box and challenge the status quo.",
